CONTROL THAT WAS WRONG: the same llama.cpp leg at max_tokens=24 (uncorrected harness)
================================================================================
 1120    0.1    34819       5     60.9       2  MISS 'The user provided a very'
 1120    0.5    34819       5     61.4       2  MISS 'We need answer just the '
 1120    0.9    34819       5     61.6       2  MISS 'The user provided a very'

0/3 passed

The three MISS rows above are not a llama.cpp retrieval failure. The model is
retrieving correctly and reasoning towards the answer; it simply has not said the
number yet within 24 tokens. This is the exact shape of the mistake that produced
the earlier false "llama.cpp fails identically, so the engine is exonerated"
conclusion: a harness limit read as a model failure.

Note the prompt-token difference: gb10 34,779 vs llama.cpp 34,819 (40 tokens), the
chat template's thinking block.
